  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To file a roof insurance claim in Utah, you can follow this step-by-step process using resources like the Legacy Roofing Utah Guide or Olympus Roofing :",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Legacy Roofing Utah Guide",
            "link": "https://www.legacyroofingutah.com/blog/roof-insurance-claim-assistance-guide"
          },
          {
            "text": "Olympus Roofing",
            "link": "https://olympusroofing.com/how-to-get-insurance-to-pay-for-roof-replacement/"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "1. Document the Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Take clear photos and videos of the roof from multiple angles (both from the ground and safely from the roof if possible).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Capture close-ups of damaged or missing shingles, dented vents, flashing, or hail hits.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Note the exact date and time the storm or damage event happened, along with local weather records.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "2. Get a Professional Inspection"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Contact a local, licensed Utah roofing contractor (such as SOS Roofing Utah or All Star Roofing ) to inspect the roof for hidden or structural damage.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "All Star Roofing",
                "link": "https://www.allstarroofpros.com/insurance-roof-claims/"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ask them for a detailed evaluation and repair or replacement estimate.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "3. Review Your Insurance Policy"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Check your deductible amount, coverage limits, and whether your policy pays Actual Cash Value (ACV) or Replacement Cost Value (RCV).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Be aware that Utah policies or laws have specific timelines for reporting storm or hail damage (often ranging from a few months up to a longer statutory window depending on policy terms).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "4. File the Claim with Your Insurer"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Call your insurance company or agent promptly to report the damage and start the formal claim.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Write down the name of the representative you spoke with, the date/time of the call, and your assigned claim number.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "5. Meet the Insurance Adjuster"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your insurance company will send an adjuster to inspect the property."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tip: Have your licensed Utah roofer present during the adjuster\u2019s inspection to point out all storm damage and make sure nothing is missed.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "6. Review the Settlement Offer"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Compare the adjuster's estimate with your contractor's quote."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "If the claim is underpaid or wrongfully denied, you can negotiate, request a re-inspection, or consult a public adjuster or policyholder advocate in Utah .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Could you tell me what kind of damage your roof has (hail, wind, leaks, or age-related wear) and who your insurance company is?\nI can give you more specific advice on what to expect."
      }
    ],
